      "text": "🇮🇷🇦🇫 Iran forcibly deports over 492,000 Afghans in 2026, UNHCR says\n\nIran has forcibly deported more than 492,000 Afghans since the start of 2026, the UN refugee agency said, Pajhwok Afghan News says.\n\nThe deportations are part of the wider departure from Iran of an estimated 581,600 Afghans who left Iran since the start of the year. That means 85% of this year's returnees were expelled rather than leaving by choice. The United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) said the influx was straining housing, basic services and job prospects in Afghanistan and adding to the burden on the communities receiving them. The flow follows 2025, when more than 1.9mn Afghans left Iran, roughly 1,261,600 of them through forced removal.\n\nThe agency's latest report, released on October 8, showed that 475,400 people crossed back into Afghanistan after February 28. Of these, 398,100 had been deported.\n\nSince the 12 Day War in June 2025, Iran has deported close to 2 million Afghan migrants after it was revealed many were recruited by the Mossad to carry out acts of sabotage against the Iranian state, assembling drones from which they struck targets from within Iran itself which was revealed to have caused most of the damage in that conflict.\n\nThe crackdown on Afghan communities in Iran after the 12 Day War pretty much destroyed Mossad's spy network in the country hence why Israel needed to enlist the U.S. for the 40-Day War in 2026.\n\n🔗 https://www.intellinews.com/iran-forcibly-deports-over-492-000-afghans-in-2026-unhcr-says-474956/",
